WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.697 --> 00:00:21.741
and I were discussing some matters of importance when our deliberations were interrupted by Thorneycroft Huxtable, the headmaster

2
00:00:21.761 --> 00:00:22.702
of the Priory School.

3
00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:25.043
He was a large man who filled the room.

4
00:00:25.764 --> 00:00:29.166
He was usually dignified so his initial behavior was rather shocking.

5
00:00:29.647 --> 00:00:34.082
Instead of presenting himself to us, he staggered against the table and then fell to the floor.

6
00:00:35.242 --> 00:00:36.663
Holmes and I sprung to our feet.

7
00:00:37.423 --> 00:00:40.885
Holmes grabbed a cushion for his head and I brought a glass of brandy to put to his

8
00:00:40.926 --> 00:00:46.469
lips. His unshaven face, his uncombed hair, and the grime on his clothes told us that he had

9
00:00:46.529 --> 00:00:48.630
traveled far and that he had left in a hurry.

10
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.591
"What's wrong?"

11
00:00:51.331 --> 00:00:51.912
asked Holmes.

12
00:00:51.932 --> 00:00:57.235
"Exhaustion; perhaps hunger and fatigue," I replied with my fingers on his pulse.

13
00:00:59.348 --> 00:01:03.930
"Ah, a train ticket from Mackleton in the north of England," said Holmes as he drew the watch

14
00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:04.570
from his pocket.

15
00:01:05.771 --> 00:01:07.051
"It's not even twelve o'clock.

16
00:01:07.551 --> 00:01:09.292
He certainly started early this morning."

17
00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:15.034
Suddenly his eyes opened, the man scrambled to his feet, and his face flushed red with shame.

18
00:01:15.054 --> 00:01:18.396
"Forgive this weakness, Mr.

19
00:01:18.436 --> 00:01:20.357
Holmes," said the man gravely.

20
00:01:20.377 --> 00:01:25.239
"I am suffering from quite a bit of stress; this is what I would like to speak about."

21
00:01:25.259 --> 00:01:28.500
"When you feel better began Holmes.

22
00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.502
"I am quite ready now," interrupted the headmaster.

23
00:01:32.522 --> 00:01:37.445
"We must be ready to leave soon, if we want to catch the next train back to Mackleton."

24
00:01:38.546 --> 00:01:43.449
Holmes looked at the headmaster and said, "I do not know the nature of your case, but we

25
00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:45.631
are currently retained in several other cases.

26
00:01:46.331 --> 00:01:48.953
Only something important "Important!"

27
00:01:49.654 --> 00:01:50.634
shouted the headmaster.

28
00:01:50.654 --> 00:01:52.615
"Of course it's important.

29
00:01:53.376 --> 00:01:56.358
The only son of the Duke of Holdernesse has been kidnapped.

30
00:01:56.818 --> 00:01:59.140
He is the wealthiest and perhaps greatest man I know.

31
00:01:59.732 --> 00:02:05.256
Furthermore, he has authorized me to offer up to ten thousand pounds to anyone who can find his

32
00:02:05.296 --> 00:02:06.917
son or name the kidnappers."

33
00:02:07.958 --> 00:02:10.419
"That's a generous offer," said Holmes.

34
00:02:10.439 --> 00:02:13.381
"Watson, I think we might just accompany Dr.

35
00:02:13.421 --> 00:02:14.422
Huxtable to the north.

36
00:02:15.022 --> 00:02:18.845
But first I must insist that you eat, and then tell us in detail what happened."

37
00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.667
After a quick breakfast, the headmaster began his story.

38
00:02:23.408 --> 00:02:26.550
He said that the duke's son was a recent arrival at the school.

39
00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:31.201
The young lord had only arrived on the first of May, the beginning of the summer term.

40
00:02:31.942 --> 00:02:35.104
He had been brought to the school by the duke's secretary, James Wilder.

41
00:02:36.004 --> 00:02:40.888
Although he thought the ten-year-old Lord Saltire was a fine boy, it was obvious to the headmaster that

42
00:02:40.908 --> 00:02:42.989
the boy had not been entirely happy at home.

43
00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:47.713
The cause of this unhappiness, according to the headmaster, was the duke's marriage.

44
00:02:48.453 --> 00:02:51.775
The duke and the duchess had separated, and she now lived in France.

45
00:02:52.676 --> 00:02:57.279
Finally, the headmaster concluded his introduction by stating that the boy had gone missing the night of the

46
00:02:57.339 --> 00:02:58.100
thirteenth of May.

47
00:02:59.456 --> 00:03:04.080
Holmes asked some questions and we learned that the boy's room was located on the second floor, and

48
00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.103
that the boy had left through his window and climbed down a stout vine.

49
00:03:07.783 --> 00:03:10.626
His disappearance was noted the following morning at seven.

50
00:03:11.286 --> 00:03:14.489
A search of his room revealed that the boy had slept in his bed and that he had

51
00:03:14.529 --> 00:03:15.490
left fully dressed.

52
00:03:16.231 --> 00:03:20.074
The room showed no signs of a struggle, so it seems that the boy had perhaps known his

53
00:03:20.114 --> 00:03:26.279
kidnapper. Soon after discovering the boy's disappearance, the headmaster learned that the German teacher and his bicycle were

54
00:03:26.379 --> 00:03:31.610
also missing; an inspection of the teacher's room had revealed that he had only been partially dressed.

55
00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:37.952
Holmes wrote several things in his notebook, looked at the headmaster and said, "You should have come to

56
00:03:37.992 --> 00:03:38.452
me sooner."

57
00:03:39.633 --> 00:03:42.554
"It's not my fault," replied the headmaster.

58
00:03:42.574 --> 00:03:44.975
"The duke wants to avoid a scandal."

59
00:03:45.835 --> 00:03:47.896
"Has there been no official investigation then?"

60
00:03:48.636 --> 00:03:49.197
asked Holmes.

61
00:03:49.217 --> 00:03:53.979
"There has, but it's been most disappointing," answered the headmaster.

62
00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:55.919
"What are their theories?"

63
00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:57.140
asked Holmes.

64
00:03:57.952 --> 00:04:02.555
The headmaster said that the police thought the German teacher's missing bicycle was a trick, and that they

65
00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:06.837
had left by some other means, and that's why the police were looking for them in Liverpool.

66
00:04:07.698 --> 00:04:11.760
Holmes didn't think that theory seemed plausible, since the hidden bike had not been found.

67
00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:18.443
Holmes was also suspicious of the police's belief that the German teacher was necessarily involved, since the boy

68
00:04:18.484 --> 00:04:20.665
had had no previous contact with this man.

69
00:04:20.685 --> 00:04:24.867
"Did the boy have any visitors before his disappearance?"

70
00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:26.228
asked Holmes.

71
00:04:27.164 --> 00:04:30.386
"No, but he did receive a letter," answered the headmaster.

72
00:04:30.406 --> 00:04:32.348
"But it was from his father."

73
00:04:32.368 --> 00:04:33.769
"Did you read it?"

74
00:04:34.329 --> 00:04:34.849
asked Holmes.

75
00:04:34.869 --> 00:04:38.432
"It is not our policy," said the headmaster.

76
00:04:38.452 --> 00:04:41.134
"How do you know it was from his father?"

77
00:04:41.974 --> 00:04:42.534
asked Holmes.

78
00:04:42.554 --> 00:04:46.837
"The duke's seal appeared on the outside," said the headmaster.

79
00:04:46.857 --> 00:04:49.979
"How was the boy's relationship with his father?

80
00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.040
Were they friendly?"

81
00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:52.341
asked Holmes.

82
00:04:53.242 --> 00:04:56.444
"The duke isn't friendly with anyone," replied the headmaster.

83
00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:59.077
"But he was always kind to the boy."

84
00:04:59.097 --> 00:05:01.938
"The boy was closer to his mother, then?"

85
00:05:02.678 --> 00:05:03.199
asked Holmes.

86
00:05:03.219 --> 00:05:05.980
"Yes," answered the headmaster.

87
00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.721
"That's what the duke's secretary had said."

88
00:05:10.162 --> 00:05:11.823
"Dr. Huxtable," said Holmes.

89
00:05:11.843 --> 00:05:15.804
"If we are going to catch that train, I think it is time for us to go."

90
00:05:15.824 --> 00:05:19.586
"Yes, quite right," said the headmaster.

91
00:05:19.606 --> 00:05:21.227
"There is a cab waiting."

92
00:05:22.147 --> 00:05:27.169
The train ride north was unremarkable, but the investigation heated up as soon as we arrived at the

93
00:05:27.209 --> 00:05:28.130
headmaster's school.

94
00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:33.972
The doorman greeted the headmaster frantically, and informed us that the duke and his secretary, Mr.

95
00:05:34.012 --> 00:05:37.373
Wilder, were here, and waiting for the headmaster's return.

96
00:05:38.414 --> 00:05:40.515
The duke and his secretary were waiting in Dr.

97
00:05:40.555 --> 00:05:41.355
Huxtable's study.

98
00:05:42.055 --> 00:05:42.836
Both were standing.

99
00:05:43.516 --> 00:05:45.036
The duke was tall and well dressed.

100
00:05:45.597 --> 00:05:47.597
A smaller, younger man stood next to him.

101
00:05:48.278 --> 00:05:49.798
I assumed it was his secretary.

102
00:05:50.459 --> 00:05:54.854
He was a nervous man but he spoke in an authoritative manner and our interview began.
